WEBVTT

00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:17.027
Gulliver's Travels by Jonathan Swift Young Adult Ailey Readers, 2012 Chapter 1 I arrive in Lilliput, myself and my family.

00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:19.197
I decide to travel.

00:00:19.258 --> 00:00:23.830
Disaster at sea, Lilliput.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:29.565
My name is Lemuel Gulliver, and this is my story.

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:35.092
My father came from the north of England and I was his middle son.

00:00:35.152 --> 00:00:39.166
I had two older brothers and two younger brothers.

00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:44.310
We didn't have much money, but my father sent me to Cambridge University.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.832
I was fourteen years old.

00:00:46.892 --> 00:00:49.123
I was very lucky.

00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:54.948
I studied hard, but after three years it was time for me to start work.

00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:58.354
I went to London to work for a famous doctor.

00:00:58.415 --> 00:01:01.650
In my free time, I studied more.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.693
I studied navigation, mathematics and medicine.

00:01:05.752 --> 00:01:07.083
Why?

00:01:07.143 --> 00:01:11.165
Because I wanted to be a doctor and I wanted to travel.

00:01:11.225 --> 00:01:17.428
I finished my studies and I found a job as a doctor on a ship called the Swallow.

00:01:17.488 --> 00:01:21.960
I traveled for three and a half years with the Swallow.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:28.787
After these three and a half years, I was tired, so I decided to stay in London.

00:01:28.847 --> 00:01:33.034
I found a small house and I found some patients.

00:01:33.094 --> 00:01:34.984
I found a wife.

00:01:35.044 --> 00:01:39.288
Her name was Mary and she had 400 pounds.

00:01:39.348 --> 00:01:42.690
But life was difficult on dry land.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.872
I was a good doctor, but I was too honest.

00:01:46.932 --> 00:01:50.544
The rich doctors in London were not very honest.

00:01:50.604 --> 00:01:53.346
They made a lot of money from their patients.

00:01:53.406 --> 00:01:56.622
They sold a lot of medicines to them.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:59.156
I didn't want to be like them.

00:01:59.216 --> 00:02:00.937
I had no choice.

00:02:00.997 --> 00:02:03.538
I had to go back to sea.

00:02:03.598 --> 00:02:08.782
For the next six years, I traveled to the East and West Indies.

00:02:08.842 --> 00:02:10.974
I made a lot of money.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:14.626
On the ship, I spent my free time reading.

00:02:14.686 --> 00:02:20.850
On dry land, I watched new people and learned new languages.

00:02:20.909 --> 00:02:25.558
I had enough money to stay at home with my wife and family.

00:02:25.618 --> 00:02:29.306
I stayed in London with them and I was happy.

00:02:29.366 --> 00:02:33.479
But three years later I had money problems again.

00:02:33.499 --> 00:02:38.552
I looked for another ship and found the antelope.

00:02:38.612 --> 00:02:42.266
Captain William Pritchard gave me a job.

00:02:42.326 --> 00:02:45.268
I was a ship's doctor again.

00:02:45.328 --> 00:02:48.410
The antelope left from Bristol on May 14, 1699.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.456
Our destination was the South Seas.

00:02:53.516 --> 00:03:01.594
The journey was comfortable, until we met a terrible storm.

00:03:01.654 --> 00:03:05.036
The ship was in danger from the strong wind.

00:03:05.096 --> 00:03:08.597
We went up and down and left and right.

00:03:08.657 --> 00:03:11.618
Twelve men died in the storm.

00:03:11.678 --> 00:03:16.040
Suddenly, the ship hit rocks near Van Demon's land.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.801
Disaster!

00:03:17.861 --> 00:03:20.548
The ship broke in two.

00:03:20.608 --> 00:03:23.634
Six of us jumped into a small boat.

00:03:23.694 --> 00:03:28.177
We tried to move away from the ship, but it was hard.

00:03:28.237 --> 00:03:33.280
We were not far from land when the wind hit our small boat.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.452
Suddenly I was in the water.

00:03:36.511 --> 00:03:40.064
I never saw my five friends again.

00:03:40.124 --> 00:03:46.938
I swam and swam for hours and hours until I was so tired that I couldn't swim.

00:03:46.998 --> 00:03:49.585
Then I relaxed.

00:03:49.645 --> 00:03:53.014
I will die here," I thought.

00:03:53.074 --> 00:03:56.706
But what was this?

00:03:56.766 --> 00:04:01.211
Suddenly, I could feel land under my feet.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.712
I felt stronger now.

00:04:03.772 --> 00:04:06.144
Now I could walk.

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:11.489
I had to walk for a long way before I arrived at the shore.

00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:16.023
It wasn't very windy now, and I could see the sun.

00:04:16.082 --> 00:04:19.288
It was about eight o'clock in the evening.

00:04:19.347 --> 00:04:24.312
I walked along the beach, looking for houses or some people.

00:04:24.371 --> 00:04:27.963
I was tired, and it was very hot.

00:04:28.023 --> 00:04:34.966
It was November, November the 5th, I think, but that was summer in the South Seas.

00:04:35.026 --> 00:04:37.707
I decided to sit down.

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:40.608
Then I lay down.

00:04:40.668 --> 00:04:43.660
The sand was warm and soft.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.612
I went to sleep.

00:04:45.672 --> 00:04:47.734
I slept for hours.

00:04:47.794 --> 00:04:50.978
I think about nine hours.

00:04:51.038 --> 00:04:54.342
When I woke up, it was light.

00:04:54.402 --> 00:04:57.704
I decided to get up and look for help.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:00.528
I couldn't move my legs.

00:05:00.588 --> 00:05:03.880
I tried to move my arms, but I couldn't.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.644
I tried to move my head, but I couldn't.

00:05:07.704 --> 00:05:11.154
The reason soon became clear.

00:05:11.214 --> 00:05:12.795
Ropes.

00:05:12.855 --> 00:05:17.776
Thousands of little ropes were over my legs and my arms.

00:05:17.836 --> 00:05:21.517
The ropes were everywhere, even in my hair.

00:05:21.577 --> 00:05:26.158
The sun was very hot and its light hurt my eyes.

00:05:26.218 --> 00:05:30.209
Then something moved on my leg.

00:05:30.269 --> 00:05:34.968
It moved across my body until I could see it.

00:05:35.028 --> 00:05:40.296
It was a little man, about six inches tall.

00:05:40.356 --> 00:05:45.567
Now I could feel another forty little men walking all over me.

00:05:45.627 --> 00:05:47.108
I shouted.

00:05:47.168 --> 00:05:49.018
They ran away.

00:05:49.078 --> 00:05:53.049
They were afraid, but so was I.

00:05:53.109 --> 00:05:55.740
They soon came back.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:02.341
One of them came up to my face again and shouted, HIKI NŌ DICK AL!

00:06:02.401 --> 00:06:05.807
His friends repeated the words.

00:06:05.867 --> 00:06:08.954
I didn't understand their language.

00:06:09.013 --> 00:06:11.164
I tried to move.

00:06:11.224 --> 00:06:17.748
I broke the little ropes on my left arm and tried to catch one of the little men.

00:06:17.808 --> 00:06:25.562
They ran away again, and then I heard a shout, TOLL GOOFONAC!

00:06:25.622 --> 00:06:30.356
Suddenly, I felt a terrible pain in my left hand.

00:06:30.416 --> 00:06:34.011
They're throwing arrows, I thought.

00:06:34.071 --> 00:06:38.578
Some arrows went into my hand, some into my body.

00:06:38.638 --> 00:06:41.119
I tried to free my hair.

00:06:41.179 --> 00:06:43.780
More terrible pain.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.464
Then the arrows stopped, so I tried to free my right arm.

00:06:49.524 --> 00:06:52.487
The arrows started again.

00:06:52.546 --> 00:06:56.018
I must stay still, I thought.

00:06:56.078 --> 00:06:58.260
I can wait until night.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.800
These people are too small to keep me here.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.560
I was right.

00:07:03.619 --> 00:07:06.532
The arrows stopped again.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:10.043
Now I could hear a lot of noise.

00:07:10.103 --> 00:07:12.584
There were more little men.

00:07:12.644 --> 00:07:15.646
What are they doing, I thought?

00:07:15.706 --> 00:07:18.278
They're building something.

00:07:18.338 --> 00:07:21.380
Again, I was right.

00:07:21.439 --> 00:07:25.032
Now I could see a platform made of wood.

00:07:25.092 --> 00:07:28.764
The platform was near my head on the right.

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:32.361
After an hour, they stopped building.

00:07:32.421 --> 00:07:38.030
Some of the little men cut the hair on my left so I could move my head.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.942
I turned my head to the right.

00:07:41.001 --> 00:07:44.804
I could see four of the little men on the platform.

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:48.506
They want to talk to me, I thought.

00:07:48.566 --> 00:07:53.099
One of the men was older and taller than the others.

00:07:53.159 --> 00:07:57.412
He started to speak, but I couldn't understand.

00:07:57.472 --> 00:08:00.294
Now I was quite hungry.

00:08:00.354 --> 00:08:03.272
I put my fingers on my mouth.

00:08:03.332 --> 00:08:05.069
The man understood.

00:08:05.089 --> 00:08:11.112
A few minutes later, I felt hundreds of the little men on my body.

00:08:11.172 --> 00:08:13.232
They had food for me.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.864
They put some in my mouth.

00:08:15.924 --> 00:08:18.515
I ate and ate.

00:08:18.575 --> 00:08:22.177
Then they brought something delicious to drink.

00:08:22.236 --> 00:08:24.828
I drank and drank.

00:08:24.888 --> 00:08:32.452
The little men were so happy that they danced on my body.

00:08:32.513 --> 00:08:38.796
Then a very important man arrived.

00:08:38.856 --> 00:08:41.606
He had a letter from the Emperor.

00:08:41.666 --> 00:08:46.988
I understood from his hands that the Emperor wanted to see me.

00:08:47.048 --> 00:08:50.258
I had to go to the capital city.

00:08:50.318 --> 00:08:53.989
I also understood that I wasn't free.

00:08:54.049 --> 00:08:57.380
Suddenly I felt tired.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.087
Why?

00:08:59.147 --> 00:09:03.376
Sleeping medicine in the wine, they told me later.

00:09:03.436 --> 00:09:06.878
I slept for about eight hours.

00:09:06.938 --> 00:09:13.142
When I woke up, I was in a strange cart on the way to the Capitol.

00:09:13.202 --> 00:09:21.468
It took 500 engineers, 900 strong men, and 1500 horses to take me there.

00:09:21.528 --> 00:09:24.450
They were very clever people.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:28.054
We arrived at the Capitol two days later.

00:09:28.114 --> 00:09:31.238
The emperor was there to meet me.

00:09:31.298 --> 00:09:35.321
This is your new home, he said.

00:09:35.381 --> 00:09:38.483
He pointed to an old church.

00:09:38.544 --> 00:09:45.039
Some of the men put new ropes on my legs, but now I could walk a little.

00:09:45.099 --> 00:09:54.150
The next morning, the emperor came to see me again with his family, with him work carts of food and drink.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:59.866
The emperor was taller than all his countrymen, and his face was strong.

00:09:59.926 --> 00:10:03.400
He was about 28 years old.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:07.392
He spoke to me, but I couldn't understand.

00:10:07.452 --> 00:10:12.616
I tried English, Dutch, Latin, French, Spanish, and Italian.

00:10:12.676 --> 00:10:19.051
No one could understand me, and after about two hours, they went away.

00:10:19.112 --> 00:10:24.028
I sat outside the church, watching some soldiers.

00:10:24.088 --> 00:10:28.531
Suddenly I felt an arrow near my eye.

00:10:28.591 --> 00:10:33.332
A group of six little men fired more arrows at me.

00:10:33.392 --> 00:10:36.783
The soldiers were angry with the little men.

00:10:36.843 --> 00:10:41.344
I picked up the six men and put five of them in my pocket.

00:10:41.404 --> 00:10:44.354
I put the other man near my mouth.

00:10:44.414 --> 00:10:47.285
Now the soldiers were worried.

00:10:47.345 --> 00:10:51.717
I put the little man down and he ran away.

00:10:51.777 --> 00:10:57.361
I don't eat little men," I said, smiling.

00:10:57.421 --> 00:11:04.496
One by one, I pulled the other little men out of my pocket and they all ran away.

00:11:04.555 --> 00:11:08.568
The soldiers were all very happy indeed.

00:11:08.628 --> 00:11:12.112
The little people began to trust me.

00:11:12.172 --> 00:11:17.724
After about two weeks, six hundred beds arrived at my new house.

00:11:17.784 --> 00:11:22.740
The little men put them all together to make one big bed.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:27.385
After that, I was very comfortable.

00:11:27.445 --> 00:11:31.748
Everybody in Lilliput now knew about me.

00:11:31.808 --> 00:11:37.352
Rich people, lazy people and curious people all came to see me.

00:11:37.412 --> 00:11:40.724
The emperor often came to see me too.

00:11:40.784 --> 00:11:45.268
He also talked to all the important people in the land.

00:11:45.328 --> 00:11:47.409
Some people were worried.

00:11:47.469 --> 00:11:50.942
My food was very expensive and I was dangerous.

00:11:51.002 --> 00:11:52.776
They wanted to kill me.

00:11:52.836 --> 00:11:55.130
The emperor said no.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.154
He remembered the six little men who fired arrows.

00:11:59.214 --> 00:12:03.018
Find me the best teachers, he said.

00:12:03.078 --> 00:12:06.641
This man must learn our language.

00:12:06.701 --> 00:12:11.996
After about three weeks, I could speak the language quite well.

00:12:12.055 --> 00:12:16.370
The emperor sometimes came to give me conversation practice.

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:21.044
Every time he came, I asked him for my freedom.

00:12:21.104 --> 00:12:25.208
Be patient, he always said.

00:12:25.267 --> 00:12:31.541
I was now very comfortable with my bed, the language and some new clothes.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:37.123
When the men brought me my new clothes, they made a list of all my things.

00:12:37.183 --> 00:12:40.875
Later that day, the emperor came to visit.

00:12:40.935 --> 00:12:44.386
He had thousands of soldiers with him.

00:12:44.446 --> 00:12:48.478
I want to take your sword, he said.

00:12:48.538 --> 00:12:52.040
I pulled out my sword slowly.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.802
The sunlight caught the sword.

00:12:54.862 --> 00:12:59.204
The light hurt the soldier's eyes and they were all afraid.

00:12:59.264 --> 00:13:05.267
I put the sword on the ground and hundreds of soldiers took it away.

00:13:05.328 --> 00:13:13.172
After that I gave my other things to the emperor, my money, my comb and my notebook.

00:13:13.233 --> 00:13:16.284
The soldiers took them all away.

00:13:16.344 --> 00:13:18.235
I was lucky.

00:13:18.295 --> 00:13:23.880
When they made the list of my things, they didn't find my secret pocket.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:28.764
In that pocket were my glasses and a pocket telescope.

00:13:28.824 --> 00:13:31.876
I didn't tell the emperor about them.

00:13:31.936 --> 00:13:36.450
I wanted to keep them for myself.

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:52.597
Chapter 2 My Life in Lilliput Lilliput Freedom War with Blafuscu escaped to Blafuscu, I returned to England.

00:13:52.657 --> 00:13:57.340
People in Lilliput seemed more friendly now.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:02.484
Boys and girls played in my hair and they called me Man Mountain.

00:14:02.544 --> 00:14:05.617
The horses weren't scared of me now.

00:14:05.677 --> 00:14:08.419
People enjoyed coming to see me.

00:14:08.479 --> 00:14:11.132
I became a tourist attraction.

00:14:11.192 --> 00:14:16.324
One day, the emperor asked me to stand up with my feet apart.

00:14:16.384 --> 00:14:20.444
Then he told his soldiers to march under me.

00:14:20.504 --> 00:14:24.014
Everyone enjoyed the parade.

00:14:24.074 --> 00:14:29.015
Now I will give you your freedom, the emperor said.

00:14:29.075 --> 00:14:31.046
But there are some rules.

00:14:31.106 --> 00:14:34.216
In fact, there are nine rules.

00:14:34.276 --> 00:14:37.817
If you agree, you will be free.

00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:41.298
The emperor gave me a piece of paper.

00:14:41.358 --> 00:14:42.848
Rules.

00:14:42.908 --> 00:14:43.910
One.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:48.304
The man mountain must not leave Lilliput without permission.

00:14:48.364 --> 00:14:49.745
2.

00:14:49.805 --> 00:14:53.748
He must not come into the city without permission.

00:14:53.808 --> 00:14:55.118
3.

00:14:55.178 --> 00:14:58.170
He must stay on the roads.

00:14:58.230 --> 00:14:59.850
4.

00:14:59.911 --> 00:15:01.962
He must be careful.

00:15:02.022 --> 00:15:03.823
Our people are very small.

00:15:03.843 --> 00:15:06.384
5.

00:15:06.445 --> 00:15:09.766
He must carry urgent messages for the Emperor.

00:15:09.786 --> 00:15:11.514
6.

00:15:11.574 --> 00:15:16.904
He must help us in our war with Blevfusco.

00:15:16.964 --> 00:15:18.476
Seven.

00:15:18.536 --> 00:15:21.958
He must help us build new houses.

00:15:22.018 --> 00:15:23.610
Eight.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:27.603
He must make a map of our country.

00:15:27.662 --> 00:15:29.634
Nine.

00:15:29.694 --> 00:15:33.057
He can have food and drink equal to 1,724 lilliputians.

00:15:33.077 --> 00:15:38.294
I had no problem with the rules.

00:15:38.354 --> 00:15:46.006
I asked a friend about the calculation for food and drink.

00:15:46.066 --> 00:15:50.710
The best mathematicians in the country decided this, he said.

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:52.932
They calculated your height.

00:15:52.992 --> 00:15:56.624
You are exactly twelve times taller than us.

00:15:56.684 --> 00:16:00.127
Your volume is therefore twelve cubed.

00:16:00.188 --> 00:16:05.232
As you know, twelve cubed equals one thousand seven hundred and twenty-four.

00:16:05.292 --> 00:16:07.782
I checked the mathematics.

00:16:07.842 --> 00:16:13.902
12 times 12 times 12 equals 1,724.

00:16:13.962 --> 00:16:17.912
You are very clever people, I answered.

00:16:17.972 --> 00:16:21.634
And very good at economics.

00:16:21.694 --> 00:16:26.525
About two weeks later, I had a visitor.

00:16:26.585 --> 00:16:31.066
His name was Reldresal and he was an important man.

00:16:31.126 --> 00:16:34.487
He sat in my hand and we talked.

00:16:34.547 --> 00:16:38.398
He told me about some of the problems in Lilliput.

00:16:38.458 --> 00:16:41.918
He was worried about political differences.

00:16:41.978 --> 00:16:46.661
He was also worried about war, war with Blevfuscu.

00:16:46.722 --> 00:16:50.804
The biggest problem, he said, is eggs.

00:16:50.864 --> 00:16:54.026
Eggs, I asked, surprised.

00:16:54.086 --> 00:16:55.916
Yes, eggs.

00:16:55.976 --> 00:16:59.308
Big Indians and little Indians.

00:16:59.368 --> 00:17:01.780
I was confused.

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:05.899
What are big Indians and little Indians?

00:17:05.959 --> 00:17:10.509
Everyone in Liddiput has boiled eggs for breakfast.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:15.054
In the past, everyone cut their boiled egg at the big end.

00:17:15.113 --> 00:17:17.226
They were big Indians.

00:17:17.286 --> 00:17:20.758
Then an emperor cut his finger.

00:17:20.819 --> 00:17:22.509
He made a law.

00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:26.494
Everyone had to cut their boiled egg at the little end.

00:17:26.554 --> 00:17:28.906
We became little Indians.

00:17:28.966 --> 00:17:32.518
Some people changed, but other people didn't.

00:17:32.578 --> 00:17:34.445
There were protests.

00:17:34.505 --> 00:17:37.601
Some big Indians left Liddyfoot.

00:17:37.661 --> 00:17:40.381
Today there are still problems.

00:17:40.441 --> 00:17:43.912
The Emperor of Blefuscu helps the big Indians.

00:17:43.972 --> 00:17:47.833
So, we are at war with Blefuscu.

00:17:47.893 --> 00:17:50.574
About eggs.

00:17:50.634 --> 00:17:52.824
Can I help?

00:17:52.884 --> 00:17:54.375
I asked.

00:17:54.435 --> 00:17:56.385
I hope so.

00:17:56.445 --> 00:17:59.186
Replied Reldrasal sadly.

00:17:59.246 --> 00:18:02.837
The Emperor of Blefuscu has a lot of ships.

00:18:02.898 --> 00:18:08.280
He has more than us, and the ships are ready to attack us.

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:12.072
Let me speak to the Emperor," I said.

00:18:12.132 --> 00:18:15.094
I had an idea.

00:18:15.154 --> 00:18:20.146
The Empire of Blevfuscu is very near to Lilliput.

00:18:20.206 --> 00:18:26.809
The channel between the two countries is less than a mile wide, and the water is not very deep.

00:18:26.869 --> 00:18:31.516
Before I went to see the Emperor, I went to the beach.

00:18:31.576 --> 00:18:36.344
I looked at the Blafuscu ships through my pocket telescope.

00:18:36.404 --> 00:18:39.436
There were about fifty ships.

00:18:39.496 --> 00:18:42.458
I went quickly to the palace.

00:18:42.518 --> 00:18:48.020
I told the emperor my idea and he was very happy indeed.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:52.042
I went home to prepare some small ropes.

00:18:52.102 --> 00:18:55.524
The next morning I went to the shore.

00:18:55.584 --> 00:19:00.029
I took off my coat and my shoes and swam across the channel.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:05.847
When I got near to the Emperor of Blevuscu's ships, his soldiers were scared.

00:19:05.908 --> 00:19:08.650
Some of them jumped into the water.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:13.434
Some of them fired arrows at me and I was worried about my eyes.

00:19:13.494 --> 00:19:17.116
Then I remembered my glasses and put them on.

00:19:17.176 --> 00:19:19.769
My job was very easy.

00:19:19.829 --> 00:19:23.682
I put ropes on all the Emperor of Blevuscu's ships.

00:19:23.742 --> 00:19:27.872
Then I pulled them across the channel to Lilliput.

00:19:27.932 --> 00:19:31.561
The Emperor of Lilliput was very happy.

00:19:31.621 --> 00:19:34.022
He gave me a special reward.

00:19:34.082 --> 00:19:38.123
I was a nardak, like a Lord, dear reader.

00:19:38.183 --> 00:19:43.455
The Emperor was so happy that he decided to send me to Blafuscu again.

00:19:43.515 --> 00:19:47.506
You can kill all the big Indians, he said.

00:19:47.566 --> 00:19:50.607
Everyone will cut their eggs from the little end.

00:19:50.667 --> 00:19:52.278
Everyone in the world!

00:19:52.338 --> 00:19:56.399
I will be Emperor of the whole world!

00:19:56.459 --> 00:20:00.571
No, that's not right, I shouted.

00:20:00.631 --> 00:20:02.392
I can't help you.

00:20:02.452 --> 00:20:04.613
I don't want to kill people.

00:20:04.673 --> 00:20:08.655
I don't want to kill people because of eggs."

00:20:08.715 --> 00:20:14.378
The Emperor was surprised, and then he was angry.

00:20:14.438 --> 00:20:19.470
Don't trust the Emperor, my friend said later that evening.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.722
Some of the Emperor's friends are angry with you.

00:20:22.782 --> 00:20:26.461
You are a nadak, and they want to be nadaks.

00:20:26.521 --> 00:20:29.690
they will say bad things about you.

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:32.872
The emperor will change."

00:20:32.932 --> 00:20:35.352
I'll be very careful.

00:20:35.413 --> 00:20:39.364
You can't always trust emperors, I said.

00:20:39.424 --> 00:20:45.228
A few weeks later, the most important lefuscans came to Lilliput.

00:20:45.288 --> 00:20:49.510
We must end the war, they said, to the emperor.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:52.042
We don't want to fight anymore.

00:20:52.102 --> 00:20:55.188
It's time for us to be friends.

00:20:55.249 --> 00:20:58.756
The emperor of Lillipot said yes.

00:20:58.816 --> 00:21:04.449
The emperor of Blafuscu had to pay a lot of money, but the war was over.

00:21:04.509 --> 00:21:08.542
There was a big dinner to celebrate the end of the war.

00:21:08.602 --> 00:21:12.654
At the dinner, I met the emperor of Blafuscu.

00:21:12.714 --> 00:21:16.596
I liked him, and I talked to him for a long time.

00:21:16.656 --> 00:21:18.418
I was lucky.

00:21:18.478 --> 00:21:22.476
He was very important to me later.

00:21:22.536 --> 00:21:27.424
Now that I was a nadak, life was different.

00:21:27.484 --> 00:21:29.866
I didn't build houses now.

00:21:29.926 --> 00:21:33.450
I had time to find out more about Lilliput.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:38.364
I talked to a lot of people, and I learned to write Lilliputian.

00:21:38.424 --> 00:21:40.896
This was very difficult.

00:21:40.956 --> 00:21:46.080
Lilliputian writing is not from the left to the right like the Europeans.

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:50.324
It is not from the right to the left like Arabic writers.

00:21:50.384 --> 00:21:55.606
It is diagonal, from one corner of the paper to the other.

00:21:55.666 --> 00:21:58.218
There are many other differences.

00:21:58.278 --> 00:22:02.390
For example, Lilliputians believe that the earth is flat.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:06.322
They also have some very strict laws.

00:22:06.382 --> 00:22:09.703
I lived very well in Lilliput.

00:22:09.764 --> 00:22:16.266
I had 300 cooks, 20 waiters, and lots and lots of other servants.

00:22:16.327 --> 00:22:18.951
People began to talk.

00:22:19.011 --> 00:22:21.936
They said I was very expensive.

00:22:21.996 --> 00:22:25.958
Many of the Emperor's friends were angry with me.

00:22:26.019 --> 00:22:29.061
They began to talk to the Emperor.

00:22:29.121 --> 00:22:30.932
My friend was right.

00:22:30.992 --> 00:22:35.206
The Emperor of Lilliput began to change.

00:22:35.266 --> 00:22:39.609
He didn't want to fight for us, one said.

00:22:39.669 --> 00:22:43.872
He talked to the Emperor of Blevver School, said another.

00:22:43.932 --> 00:22:48.756
He wants to live in Blevver School, said a third man.

00:22:48.816 --> 00:22:50.737
Oh, no!

00:22:50.797 --> 00:22:51.968
You're right!"

00:22:52.029 --> 00:22:53.210
said the Emperor.

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:55.501
He will fight against us.

00:22:55.562 --> 00:22:58.234
We must kill him.

00:22:58.294 --> 00:23:03.118
Later that night, my good friend came to see me.

00:23:03.178 --> 00:23:06.772
You must leave Lilliput, he said.

00:23:06.832 --> 00:23:09.304
I know, I answered.

00:23:09.364 --> 00:23:12.117
It's too dangerous for me here.

00:23:12.178 --> 00:23:14.955
We made a plan.

00:23:15.015 --> 00:23:20.062
That night, I said goodbye to my lilyputian friend.

00:23:20.123 --> 00:23:22.513
I swam to Blefuscu.

00:23:22.573 --> 00:23:25.804
I took a ship and put my things in it.

00:23:25.865 --> 00:23:29.066
I pulled the ship across the channel with me.

00:23:29.125 --> 00:23:32.847
The people of Blefuscu were very pleased to see me.

00:23:32.907 --> 00:23:36.688
They sent a message to the emperor of Blefuscu.

00:23:36.748 --> 00:23:41.590
Almost immediately, the emperor and his wife arrived at the shore.

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:45.918
The people of Blefuscu were not scared of me.

00:23:45.978 --> 00:23:51.187
The emperor was very kind to me, but there was one problem.

00:23:51.247 --> 00:23:56.468
There was no house for me in Blofuscu, so I slept outside.

00:23:56.529 --> 00:24:01.210
Three days after my arrival, I went for a walk.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:04.471
I went to the northeast of the island.

00:24:04.531 --> 00:24:07.432
I saw something in the sea.

00:24:07.492 --> 00:24:09.472
Was it a boat?

00:24:09.532 --> 00:24:13.624
I took off my coat and shoes and swam to it.

00:24:13.684 --> 00:24:15.586
It was a boat.

00:24:15.646 --> 00:24:19.660
an empty boat and it was my size.

00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:24.602
I swam back to the shore and went immediately to the city.

00:24:24.662 --> 00:24:27.732
I asked for a meeting with the Emperor.

00:24:27.792 --> 00:24:30.664
He was happy to see me.

00:24:30.724 --> 00:24:33.895
Your Majesty, I began.

00:24:33.955 --> 00:24:35.946
I need your help.

00:24:36.006 --> 00:24:39.808
I will help you if I can," he answered.

00:24:39.868 --> 00:24:42.158
Thank you, Your Majesty.

00:24:42.218 --> 00:24:46.485
I need twenty ships and three thousand men.

00:24:46.545 --> 00:24:49.400
The emperor was surprised.

00:24:49.460 --> 00:24:51.041
Why?

00:24:51.101 --> 00:24:54.912
There is a large boat in the sea in the northeast.

00:24:54.972 --> 00:24:57.702
I need your help to bring it here.

00:24:57.762 --> 00:25:01.774
I can use the boat to return to my country.

00:25:01.834 --> 00:25:04.894
The emperor was very kind.

00:25:04.954 --> 00:25:07.905
He gave me the ships and the men.

00:25:07.965 --> 00:25:11.736
We brought the boat back to Blevfusco.

00:25:11.796 --> 00:25:17.036
Before I left, the emperor received a letter from Lilliput.

00:25:17.096 --> 00:25:21.428
The emperor of Lilliput was very, very angry.

00:25:21.488 --> 00:25:26.120
Send the man mountain back to Lilliput, he wrote.

00:25:26.180 --> 00:25:29.881
The emperor of Blevusgu sent a letter back.

00:25:29.941 --> 00:25:35.734
I'm very sorry, he wrote, but I cannot send him back to you.

00:25:35.794 --> 00:25:38.514
The man mountain is very kind.

00:25:38.574 --> 00:25:40.766
He is a peaceful man.

00:25:40.826 --> 00:25:43.876
He stopped the war between us.

00:25:43.936 --> 00:25:47.310
The emperor showed me his letter.

00:25:47.370 --> 00:25:50.842
He asked me to stay in Blefuscu.

00:25:50.902 --> 00:25:54.144
I will protect you, he said.

00:25:54.204 --> 00:25:58.856
No, I must leave, I answered.

00:25:58.916 --> 00:26:01.498
The emperor helped me.

00:26:01.558 --> 00:26:04.819
He gave me food and drink for the journey.

00:26:04.880 --> 00:26:07.501
He also gave me some money.

00:26:07.561 --> 00:26:11.984
I took some of the little animals with me to show people at home.

00:26:12.044 --> 00:26:17.840
I wanted to take some of the little men with me too, but the emperor said no.

00:26:17.900 --> 00:26:26.239
On the 24th of September 1701 at 6 in the morning, I left Blevfescue.

00:26:26.299 --> 00:26:30.022
My journey was very comfortable.

00:26:30.082 --> 00:26:33.094
The first day, the weather was good.

00:26:33.154 --> 00:26:37.658
I stopped near a small island and slept for a few hours.

00:26:37.718 --> 00:26:40.440
The next day was the same.

00:26:40.500 --> 00:26:46.656
On the third day, at about 3 o'clock in the afternoon, I saw a ship.

00:26:46.716 --> 00:26:50.450
To my surprise, the ship was English.

00:26:50.510 --> 00:26:54.022
I reached the ship about two hours later.

00:26:54.082 --> 00:26:57.664
The captain was a very kind man.

00:26:57.724 --> 00:26:59.595
Where are you going?

00:26:59.655 --> 00:27:00.696
I asked.

00:27:00.756 --> 00:27:02.948
England, he answered.

00:27:03.008 --> 00:27:05.829
We are returning from Japan.

00:27:05.890 --> 00:27:10.392
Everyone on the ship was curious about my story.

00:27:10.452 --> 00:27:14.766
They didn't believe that the people on Lilliput were so small.

00:27:14.826 --> 00:27:17.828
You're mad, they said.

00:27:17.888 --> 00:27:21.721
Let me show you something," I answered.

00:27:21.782 --> 00:27:24.854
I showed them my little animals.

00:27:24.914 --> 00:27:27.556
Now they believed me.

00:27:27.616 --> 00:27:32.610
The journey was very comfortable, and we soon arrived home.

00:27:32.670 --> 00:27:36.142
I made a lot of money with my little animals.

00:27:36.202 --> 00:27:40.436
I took them to markets in London, and I showed them to people.

00:27:40.496 --> 00:27:43.278
People paid a lot to see them.

00:27:43.338 --> 00:27:47.032
Then I sold them for a hundred pounds.

00:27:47.092 --> 00:27:50.156
Now I was rich.

00:27:50.216 --> 00:27:55.416
I stayed with my wife and family, and I bought a new house.

00:27:55.476 --> 00:27:58.397
But I didn't want to stay in England.

00:27:58.457 --> 00:28:00.697
I wanted to travel.

00:28:00.757 --> 00:28:04.408
I gave my wife 1,500 pounds.

00:28:04.468 --> 00:28:08.828
I said goodbye to her, my son, and my daughter.

00:28:08.888 --> 00:28:11.599
We were all very sad.

00:28:11.659 --> 00:28:13.970
I left England again.

00:28:14.030 --> 00:28:17.974
The name of my ship was the adventure.

00:28:18.034 --> 00:28:25.404
I will tell you all about my adventures on the adventure in the next chapter.

00:28:25.464 --> 00:28:33.910
Chapter 3 My Journey to Broading Nag I go back to sea.

00:28:33.970 --> 00:28:36.984
I arrive at the land of giants.

00:28:37.044 --> 00:28:40.076
I become a tourist attraction.

00:28:40.136 --> 00:28:44.189
I live with the king and queen.

00:28:44.249 --> 00:28:51.604
On the 20th of June, 1702, I left England on the adventure.

00:28:51.664 --> 00:28:57.618
We had a very good journey south and spent the winter at the Cape of Good Hope.

00:28:57.678 --> 00:29:00.652
In the spring, we sailed again.

00:29:00.712 --> 00:29:05.354
We passed Madagascar and sailed towards the Moluca Islands.

00:29:05.414 --> 00:29:08.026
The weather was very calm.

00:29:08.086 --> 00:29:09.948
Too calm.

00:29:10.008 --> 00:29:13.430
Captain Nicholas was a very good sailor.

00:29:13.490 --> 00:29:15.790
He understood weather.

00:29:15.850 --> 00:29:21.860
There will be a terrible storm tomorrow among soon," he said one day.

00:29:21.920 --> 00:29:24.211
He was right.

00:29:24.271 --> 00:29:27.492
The storm continued for days.

00:29:27.552 --> 00:29:30.023
No one knew where we were.

00:29:30.083 --> 00:29:34.435
We had lots of food, but we didn't have much water.

00:29:34.495 --> 00:29:37.696
We started to look for land.

00:29:37.756 --> 00:29:42.451
On the 16th of June, 1703, we saw land.

00:29:42.511 --> 00:29:47.946
Some of us got into a small boat and went towards the shore.

00:29:48.006 --> 00:29:51.947
When we arrived, we started to look for water.

00:29:52.007 --> 00:29:54.758
We went in different directions.

00:29:54.818 --> 00:29:59.839
I didn't see any people, and I didn't find any water.

00:29:59.899 --> 00:30:04.640
I was tired, so I started to go back to the boat.

00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:09.382
When I got back to the shore, I couldn't see the boat.

00:30:09.442 --> 00:30:11.584
Then I saw it.

00:30:11.644 --> 00:30:14.948
at sea, moving quickly.

00:30:15.008 --> 00:30:20.772
Behind it, there was a very tall man, a giant.

00:30:20.832 --> 00:30:24.556
He tried but couldn't catch the boat.

00:30:24.616 --> 00:30:28.870
I ran in the opposite direction.

00:30:28.930 --> 00:30:32.482
I ran for miles.

00:30:32.542 --> 00:30:35.044
I arrived at a field.

00:30:35.104 --> 00:30:39.938
The field was full of wheat, but it was very, very tall.

00:30:39.998 --> 00:30:45.542
Suddenly another giant man appeared, then another, then a woman.

00:30:45.602 --> 00:30:47.964
There were seven of them.

00:30:48.024 --> 00:30:51.256
What are they doing, I thought?

00:30:51.316 --> 00:30:53.528
They're farmers.

00:30:53.588 --> 00:30:57.361
Oh no, they're cutting the wheat.

00:30:57.421 --> 00:31:01.944
I ran and ran, but the farmers came nearer.

00:31:02.004 --> 00:31:05.000
I stopped, very tired.

00:31:05.060 --> 00:31:07.674
My wife, I thought.

00:31:07.734 --> 00:31:11.155
My poor wife and my poor children.

00:31:11.215 --> 00:31:13.506
Why did I leave England?

00:31:13.566 --> 00:31:16.696
I don't want to die here.

00:31:16.756 --> 00:31:20.737
I thought about Lilliput and the little people.

00:31:20.797 --> 00:31:23.028
They were scared of me.

00:31:23.088 --> 00:31:27.418
Now I was scared of someone much bigger than me.

00:31:27.479 --> 00:31:31.319
At that very moment, I saw a foot.

00:31:31.379 --> 00:31:32.410
No!

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:33.490
Help!

00:31:33.550 --> 00:31:35.054
Stop!

00:31:35.114 --> 00:31:37.730
I shouted loudly.

00:31:37.790 --> 00:31:40.482
The farmer stopped.

00:31:40.542 --> 00:31:43.776
He looked at the ground in front of him.

00:31:43.836 --> 00:31:46.358
Then he saw me.

00:31:46.418 --> 00:31:49.120
He looked at me for a while.

00:31:49.180 --> 00:31:51.392
I understood his thoughts.

00:31:51.452 --> 00:31:54.686
I looked like this when I see a strange animal.

00:31:54.746 --> 00:31:58.158
Will it hurt me, I think?

00:31:58.218 --> 00:32:02.750
After a while, he picked me up carefully.

00:32:02.810 --> 00:32:06.611
He held me between his thumb and a finger.

00:32:06.671 --> 00:32:08.592
I was scared.

00:32:08.652 --> 00:32:11.564
I was very high in the air.

00:32:11.625 --> 00:32:13.585
Don't drop me!

00:32:13.605 --> 00:32:15.296
I shouted.

00:32:15.356 --> 00:32:16.377
Ouch!

00:32:16.437 --> 00:32:18.798
You're hurting me!

00:32:18.858 --> 00:32:21.830
He seemed to understand.

00:32:21.890 --> 00:32:25.052
The farmer put me into his pocket.

00:32:25.112 --> 00:32:28.034
He walked towards his friends.

00:32:28.094 --> 00:32:30.066
Look at this!"

00:32:30.126 --> 00:32:31.698
I think he said.

00:32:31.758 --> 00:32:35.500
I didn't understand the language, but I could guess.

00:32:35.560 --> 00:32:38.332
The farmer put me on the ground.

00:32:38.392 --> 00:32:41.326
His friend sat down in a circle.

00:32:41.386 --> 00:32:42.996
They watched me.

00:32:43.056 --> 00:32:45.388
I tried to talk to them.

00:32:45.448 --> 00:32:48.371
I tried many different languages.

00:32:48.431 --> 00:32:52.441
They couldn't really hear me, and they couldn't understand.

00:32:52.501 --> 00:32:57.731
The farmers tried to talk to me, but the noise was very loud.

00:32:57.791 --> 00:33:00.173
It hurt my ears.

00:33:00.232 --> 00:33:04.996
After a while, the farmer carried me to his house.

00:33:05.056 --> 00:33:07.257
He was very careful.

00:33:07.317 --> 00:33:09.218
He called his wife.

00:33:09.279 --> 00:33:12.170
She was scared and ran away.

00:33:12.231 --> 00:33:17.673
She came back after a minute or two and was very kind to me.

00:33:17.734 --> 00:33:23.238
It was lunchtime, and she put a very big dish onto the table.

00:33:23.298 --> 00:33:25.772
The family came to eat.

00:33:25.832 --> 00:33:28.504
They were very curious.

00:33:28.564 --> 00:33:35.880
In total, there were the farmer and his wife, their three children and an old grandmother.

00:33:35.940 --> 00:33:39.854
The farmer's wife gave me some food and drink.

00:33:39.914 --> 00:33:45.238
Suddenly, a giant cat jumped up to sit on the wife's knees.

00:33:45.298 --> 00:33:50.930
I was scared for a moment, but I think the cat was more afraid of me.

00:33:50.990 --> 00:33:56.568
After the meal, the nurse came into the room with the farmer's enormous baby.

00:33:56.628 --> 00:33:59.329
This was a terrible moment.

00:33:59.390 --> 00:34:02.892
The baby saw me and immediately picked me up.

00:34:02.952 --> 00:34:05.202
He put me into his mouth.

00:34:05.262 --> 00:34:07.214
I was very lucky.

00:34:07.274 --> 00:34:11.056
The farmer's wife pulled my legs and I was free.

00:34:11.116 --> 00:34:16.358
Then the farmer's wife took me upstairs and put me into a bedroom.

00:34:16.418 --> 00:34:18.538
She locked the door.

00:34:18.598 --> 00:34:21.682
I slept for about two hours.

00:34:21.742 --> 00:34:26.144
When I woke up, I looked around the room.

00:34:26.204 --> 00:34:31.126
Then I saw them, two enormous rats.

00:34:31.186 --> 00:34:33.537
They wanted to eat me.

00:34:33.596 --> 00:34:37.328
I took out my sword and killed the first one.

00:34:37.388 --> 00:34:39.888
The second ran away.

00:34:39.948 --> 00:34:45.789
The farmer's wife came in at that moment and saved me.

00:34:45.850 --> 00:34:50.110
I liked the farmer's daughter very much.

00:34:50.170 --> 00:34:54.841
She was nine years old and about forty feet tall.

00:34:54.901 --> 00:34:57.462
She made a little bed for me.

00:34:57.522 --> 00:35:01.232
She also made seven little shirts for me.

00:35:01.292 --> 00:35:03.873
She was my teacher too.

00:35:03.933 --> 00:35:08.444
Very quickly I began to understand their language.

00:35:08.504 --> 00:35:12.265
She called me Grildrig, little man.

00:35:12.325 --> 00:35:15.870
Everyone in the family then called me Grildrig.

00:35:15.930 --> 00:35:20.356
Soon, everyone in the country called me Grildrig.

00:35:20.417 --> 00:35:26.332
Her name was Glumdow Klitch, and she was very, very kind to me.

00:35:26.392 --> 00:35:32.096
Glumdow Klitch stayed with me all the time I was in Broading Nag.

00:35:32.156 --> 00:35:35.728
Everyone in the village knew about me.

00:35:35.788 --> 00:35:41.579
I was a strange animal, just like a human, but very small.

00:35:41.639 --> 00:35:46.938
When visitors came to the house, the farmer put me on the table.

00:35:46.998 --> 00:35:50.262
I spoke to the people in their language.

00:35:50.322 --> 00:35:53.984
One visitor made a suggestion to the farmer.

00:35:54.044 --> 00:35:56.897
Put him in a box and take him to the market.

00:35:56.957 --> 00:36:00.040
People will pay to see him, he said.

00:36:00.100 --> 00:36:02.672
Glumdowclich was afraid.

00:36:02.732 --> 00:36:05.944
Don't hurt him, she said.

00:36:06.004 --> 00:36:11.204
The next day, the farmer put me in a box to take me to the market.

00:36:11.264 --> 00:36:13.828
Glumdalklitch came with us.

00:36:13.888 --> 00:36:17.750
The journey was uncomfortable in my little box.

00:36:17.810 --> 00:36:22.792
When we arrived at the village, the farmer found a room at a hotel.

00:36:22.852 --> 00:36:25.372
He brought people to see me.

00:36:25.432 --> 00:36:30.294
Glumdalklitch asked me questions and I answered in their language.

00:36:30.354 --> 00:36:33.455
A schoolboy threw a peanut at me.

00:36:33.515 --> 00:36:35.095
It didn't hit me.

00:36:35.155 --> 00:36:37.536
I was very lucky.

00:36:37.596 --> 00:36:40.525
The farmer was very happy.

00:36:40.585 --> 00:36:46.215
He decided to take me to all the markets in Brotting Nag.

00:36:46.275 --> 00:36:52.038
Traveling was very difficult for me and very uncomfortable.

00:36:52.098 --> 00:36:53.918
I became ill.

00:36:53.978 --> 00:36:56.469
The farmer was not worried.

00:36:56.529 --> 00:37:00.770
I must sell him before he dies, he thought.

00:37:00.830 --> 00:37:04.732
Luckily, a message came from the Queen.

00:37:04.792 --> 00:37:09.171
She wanted to see me immediately, so we went to the palace.

00:37:09.231 --> 00:37:11.560
She was very kind.

00:37:11.620 --> 00:37:13.411
Where are you from?

00:37:13.471 --> 00:37:14.862
She asked.

00:37:14.922 --> 00:37:17.924
England, I replied.

00:37:17.984 --> 00:37:21.697
And why did you come to Broadingnag?

00:37:21.757 --> 00:37:24.590
I told her about my travels.

00:37:24.650 --> 00:37:27.572
The queen was very interested.

00:37:27.632 --> 00:37:30.524
She decided to buy me.

00:37:30.584 --> 00:37:33.276
How much must I give you?

00:37:33.336 --> 00:37:35.388
She asked the farmer.

00:37:35.448 --> 00:37:39.456
A thousand gold pieces, he answered.

00:37:39.516 --> 00:37:45.246
Your Majesty," I said, yes, Grildrig?

00:37:45.306 --> 00:37:47.456
I have one question.

00:37:47.516 --> 00:37:49.998
Can Glum Dalclich come too?

00:37:50.058 --> 00:37:52.850
She is my nurse and my teacher.

00:37:52.910 --> 00:37:59.144
Glum Dalclich was happy, the queen was happy, and the farmer was happy.

00:37:59.204 --> 00:38:04.708
He was rich, and his daughter lived in the royal palace.

00:38:04.768 --> 00:38:09.212
One day, the queen took me to see the king.

00:38:09.272 --> 00:38:11.534
He was surprised.

00:38:11.594 --> 00:38:13.925
Is that your new pet?

00:38:13.985 --> 00:38:16.446
He asked, what is it?

00:38:16.506 --> 00:38:19.757
He's not an animal, she answered.

00:38:19.818 --> 00:38:21.228
Listen.

00:38:21.288 --> 00:38:26.740
The queen asked me some questions, and I answered in her language.

00:38:26.800 --> 00:38:30.332
The king was interested in my story too.

00:38:30.392 --> 00:38:32.824
He called Glumdalclich.

00:38:32.884 --> 00:38:35.324
Is his story true?

00:38:35.384 --> 00:38:36.745
He asked.

00:38:36.805 --> 00:38:39.654
Yes, she answered.

00:38:39.714 --> 00:38:43.003
At first, the king was not sure.

00:38:43.063 --> 00:38:46.124
Perhaps I was a clockwork toy.

00:38:46.184 --> 00:38:50.856
So he called the three most intelligent people in broadening nag.

00:38:50.916 --> 00:38:54.517
They looked at me, and they talked to me.

00:38:54.577 --> 00:38:56.688
He isn't an animal.

00:38:56.708 --> 00:39:02.120
He isn't fast, and he can't climb trees, one said.

00:39:02.180 --> 00:39:05.791
He isn't a man, said another.

00:39:05.851 --> 00:39:08.145
He's too small.

00:39:08.206 --> 00:39:13.012
He's a freak, a freak of nature, they all said.

00:39:13.072 --> 00:39:17.816
Your Majesty, I shouted, I'm a man.

00:39:17.876 --> 00:39:20.888
I come from a country called England.

00:39:20.948 --> 00:39:24.430
In England there are millions of men and women like me.

00:39:24.490 --> 00:39:29.914
In my country the trees and the animals are in proportion to us.

00:39:29.974 --> 00:39:35.138
The three intelligent people laughed at me.

00:39:35.198 --> 00:39:38.502
The king was a fair man.

00:39:38.562 --> 00:39:41.654
He was still interested in my story.

00:39:41.714 --> 00:39:45.326
Look after him, he said to the Queen.

00:39:45.386 --> 00:39:49.216
Give him food, build a house for him.

00:39:49.276 --> 00:39:51.467
I like him.

00:39:51.527 --> 00:39:54.568
The Queen called a carpenter.

00:39:54.628 --> 00:39:59.608
Make a beautiful house for this man, she said.

00:39:59.668 --> 00:40:02.929
The carpenter was very clever.

00:40:02.989 --> 00:40:06.448
He made a very comfortable box for me.

00:40:06.508 --> 00:40:12.117
It had windows, a bed, chairs, a table, and a wardrobe.

00:40:12.177 --> 00:40:16.168
It was perfect for traveling and for living.

00:40:16.228 --> 00:40:18.658
The queen liked me.

00:40:18.718 --> 00:40:21.198
I always had dinner with her.

00:40:21.259 --> 00:40:28.780
She found toys, silver plates, knives and forks for me, and she cut my food for me.

00:40:28.840 --> 00:40:33.101
Every Wednesday, Wednesdays were holidays.

00:40:33.161 --> 00:40:35.814
The king and queen had lunch together.

00:40:35.874 --> 00:40:38.516
The King liked talking to me.

00:40:38.576 --> 00:40:42.128
He talked about my country and Europe.

00:40:42.188 --> 00:40:47.119
He asked about government, laws, religion and education.

00:40:47.179 --> 00:40:52.310
Sometimes he laughed, but he always listened.

00:40:52.370 --> 00:40:58.172
Sometimes life in broadening nag was dangerous for a little man.

00:40:58.232 --> 00:41:03.898
One day I opened my window and there were twenty giant wasps outside.

00:41:03.958 --> 00:41:06.596
Luckily I had my sword.

00:41:06.656 --> 00:41:11.570
They attacked me, so I killed them all, one by one.

00:41:11.630 --> 00:41:15.012
I kept some wasps' dings as souvenirs.

00:41:15.072 --> 00:41:18.775
I had problems with giant flies too.

00:41:18.835 --> 00:41:22.528
I often traveled with the king and queen.

00:41:22.588 --> 00:41:25.860
Broading nag was a very large country.

00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:29.234
European map makers are very bad.

00:41:29.294 --> 00:41:34.480
They think there is no large country between Japan and California.

00:41:34.540 --> 00:41:40.223
When I return to England, I will correct their maps, I thought.

00:41:40.283 --> 00:41:45.504
The mountains in the north of Brodynag are 30 miles high.

00:41:45.564 --> 00:41:49.544
People catch fish in the rivers, not in the sea.

00:41:49.604 --> 00:41:50.825
Why?

00:41:50.885 --> 00:41:53.935
Because the fish in the sea are too small.

00:41:53.995 --> 00:41:57.526
In fact, they are just like ours in England.

00:41:57.586 --> 00:42:03.630
There are 51 cities in Brodynag and a very large number of villages.

00:42:03.690 --> 00:42:10.316
The cities are very beautiful, and there are a lot of royal palaces and temples.

00:42:10.376 --> 00:42:13.728
The king began to trust me.

00:42:13.788 --> 00:42:17.350
He often asked questions about England.

00:42:17.410 --> 00:42:24.403
We have two islands, and we have some land in another country, America, I said.

00:42:24.463 --> 00:42:26.994
We have a king and a parliament.

00:42:27.054 --> 00:42:32.936
Parliament has two houses, the House of Lords and the House of Commons.

00:42:32.996 --> 00:42:35.104
We also have judges.

00:42:35.164 --> 00:42:37.465
We pay tax to the government.

00:42:37.525 --> 00:42:41.696
We have very good soldiers and very good sailors.

00:42:41.756 --> 00:42:44.358
Why do you need soldiers?

00:42:44.418 --> 00:42:45.548
He asked.

00:42:45.608 --> 00:42:48.009
Soldiers are very expensive.

00:42:48.069 --> 00:42:51.000
Farmers are better for the country.

00:42:51.060 --> 00:42:55.531
We are a very powerful country, I explained.

00:42:55.591 --> 00:42:58.045
We have very good guns.

00:42:58.105 --> 00:43:02.070
We can kill a lot of people in a very short time.

00:43:02.130 --> 00:43:05.070
So we stay powerful.

00:43:05.130 --> 00:43:08.392
I can help you make guns like ours.

00:43:08.452 --> 00:43:11.133
The king was very angry.

00:43:11.193 --> 00:43:13.424
No, he shouted.

00:43:13.484 --> 00:43:16.816
I love science and I love art.

00:43:16.876 --> 00:43:21.918
My people study mathematics, philosophy, history and poetry.

00:43:21.978 --> 00:43:25.339
I think you are horrible people.

00:43:25.399 --> 00:43:28.658
You make war on other countries for power.

00:43:28.718 --> 00:43:31.666
I don't make war on other countries.

00:43:31.726 --> 00:43:35.738
I don't need big guns to kill other people.

00:43:35.798 --> 00:43:39.340
I need farmers to grow food for them."

00:43:39.400 --> 00:43:44.263
We didn't speak about England again.

00:43:44.323 --> 00:43:47.505
Chapter 4.

00:43:47.565 --> 00:43:50.186
I travel to La Puta.

00:43:50.246 --> 00:43:52.538
I leave Brodynag.

00:43:52.598 --> 00:43:54.629
I return to England.

00:43:54.689 --> 00:43:56.815
I meet pirates.

00:43:56.876 --> 00:44:01.393
I visit the flying island of La Puta.

00:44:01.453 --> 00:44:07.986
After two years in broading nag, I began to think about my freedom.

00:44:08.046 --> 00:44:10.217
It seemed impossible.

00:44:10.277 --> 00:44:14.179
Everyone was so big, and I was so small.

00:44:14.239 --> 00:44:20.482
At the beginning of the third year, the king and queen decided to travel to the south coast.

00:44:20.542 --> 00:44:23.496
They wanted to visit their people there.

00:44:23.556 --> 00:44:28.031
I traveled with them in my now very comfortable box.

00:44:28.091 --> 00:44:30.872
Glumdalklitch came too.

00:44:30.932 --> 00:44:36.726
At the end of our journey to the south, Glumdalklitch and I were very tired.

00:44:36.786 --> 00:44:40.947
I had a cold, and Glumdalklitch was very ill.

00:44:41.008 --> 00:44:45.890
I wanted some fresh air, but Glumdalklitch wanted to sleep.

00:44:45.950 --> 00:44:48.011
She called a boy.

00:44:48.072 --> 00:44:52.007
Take Grildrig to the sea, she said.

00:44:52.068 --> 00:44:56.676
I don't feel very well, so I will stay here.

00:44:56.736 --> 00:44:59.208
Be very careful.

00:44:59.268 --> 00:45:02.510
Look after Grildrick well."

00:45:02.570 --> 00:45:06.194
Glum downclich was very sad.

00:45:06.254 --> 00:45:10.036
Perhaps she could see into the future.

00:45:10.096 --> 00:45:15.110
The boy carried me, in my box, down to the sea.

00:45:15.170 --> 00:45:17.552
It took about half an hour.

00:45:17.612 --> 00:45:21.274
I was very tired, and I fell asleep.

00:45:21.334 --> 00:45:24.424
I don't really know what happened next.

00:45:24.484 --> 00:45:26.716
Perhaps the boy went swimming.

00:45:26.776 --> 00:45:29.959
Perhaps he put the box down just for a minute.

00:45:30.019 --> 00:45:32.870
But suddenly I woke up.

00:45:32.930 --> 00:45:34.622
What's this?

00:45:34.682 --> 00:45:37.064
Why is the box moving so fast?

00:45:37.124 --> 00:45:38.455
I thought.

00:45:38.515 --> 00:45:40.716
I was scared.

00:45:40.777 --> 00:45:43.108
I looked out of my window.

00:45:43.168 --> 00:45:46.260
I could see sky and clouds.

00:45:46.321 --> 00:45:49.669
I was now very high in the sky.

00:45:49.729 --> 00:45:54.276
I was in the claws of a giant bird.

00:45:54.336 --> 00:45:56.796
It knows I'm in here.

00:45:56.856 --> 00:46:00.377
It will eat me, I thought, afraid.

00:46:00.437 --> 00:46:02.337
Help!

00:46:02.397 --> 00:46:04.128
I shouted out of the window.

00:46:04.148 --> 00:46:06.928
Help!

00:46:06.988 --> 00:46:11.229
Suddenly, the box began to fall.

00:46:11.289 --> 00:46:14.039
It fell down and down.

00:46:14.099 --> 00:46:19.371
With a splash, it fell into the sea.

00:46:19.432 --> 00:46:26.547
In the water, in the box, I thought about poor Glumdowclich.

00:46:26.607 --> 00:46:29.339
I thought about the king and queen.

00:46:29.399 --> 00:46:34.923
Please don't be angry with Glumdowclich, I said to myself.

00:46:34.983 --> 00:46:38.496
Then I thought about my situation.

00:46:38.556 --> 00:46:41.098
Will someone rescue me?

00:46:41.158 --> 00:46:44.800
Will I die in the water here?

00:46:44.860 --> 00:46:49.808
After about four scary hours, I heard a noise.

00:46:49.868 --> 00:46:51.604
It was a ship.

00:46:51.664 --> 00:46:52.935
Help!

00:46:52.995 --> 00:46:54.426
Help!

00:46:54.486 --> 00:46:56.068
I shouted.

00:46:56.128 --> 00:46:57.890
Who's there?

00:46:57.950 --> 00:47:00.382
A man answered in English.

00:47:00.442 --> 00:47:02.644
Lemuel Gulliver!

00:47:02.704 --> 00:47:05.866
I shouted, Help me please!

00:47:05.926 --> 00:47:11.380
The ship's carpenter made a hole in the box, and I walked out.

00:47:11.440 --> 00:47:14.353
The sailors were very surprised.

00:47:14.414 --> 00:47:16.986
They seemed small to me.

00:47:17.046 --> 00:47:19.558
Was I back in Liddyput?

00:47:19.618 --> 00:47:25.071
No, they were the same size as me.

00:47:25.131 --> 00:47:29.502
The destination of the ship was England.

00:47:29.562 --> 00:47:33.612
On the journey, I spent a lot of time with the captain.

00:47:33.672 --> 00:47:36.243
I told him about Brodingnag.

00:47:36.303 --> 00:47:38.184
He didn't believe me.

00:47:38.244 --> 00:47:41.094
You're mad, he said.

00:47:41.154 --> 00:47:46.630
Luckily, I had the wasp sting and some other souvenirs of Brodingnag.

00:47:46.690 --> 00:47:50.336
When he saw them, he believed my story.

00:47:50.396 --> 00:47:53.588
Write a book about it, he said.

00:47:53.648 --> 00:47:57.029
Perhaps I will, I answered.

00:47:57.090 --> 00:48:03.714
I arrived home on the 3rd of June, 1703, about nine months later.

00:48:03.774 --> 00:48:06.996
My wife was very happy to see me.

00:48:07.056 --> 00:48:11.268
My wife and daughter seemed very small to me.

00:48:11.328 --> 00:48:15.721
You will never go to see again, she said.

00:48:15.781 --> 00:48:18.614
she was wrong.

00:48:18.674 --> 00:48:23.598
Ten days later, a man came to my house.

00:48:23.658 --> 00:48:29.672
His name was William Robinson, and he was the captain of the Hopewell.

00:48:29.732 --> 00:48:32.604
He was like a brother to me.

00:48:32.665 --> 00:48:35.466
He came to visit me often.

00:48:35.526 --> 00:48:39.640
One day he said, I want to go to India.

00:48:39.700 --> 00:48:41.458
Will you come with me?

00:48:41.518 --> 00:48:43.956
I need a good ship's doctor?"

00:48:44.016 --> 00:48:46.067
Yes, I said.

00:48:46.127 --> 00:48:49.178
I'll be very happy to come with you.

00:48:49.238 --> 00:48:55.009
On the 5th of August, 1706, we left England again.

00:48:55.069 --> 00:48:59.360
In April, the next year, we arrived in Madras.

00:48:59.420 --> 00:49:04.452
We stayed there for a few weeks because some sailors were ill.

00:49:04.512 --> 00:49:08.962
When we set off again, there was a terrible storm.

00:49:09.022 --> 00:49:11.719
We didn't know where we were.

00:49:11.779 --> 00:49:16.068
On the tenth day, pirates saw our ship.

00:49:16.128 --> 00:49:20.662
Some of the pirates were Dutch, and some were Japanese.

00:49:20.722 --> 00:49:27.967
I spoke Dutch quite well, so said, Please, take the ship, but don't kill us.

00:49:28.028 --> 00:49:31.360
The Japanese pirate was angry.

00:49:31.420 --> 00:49:34.843
Put him in a canoe, alone, he said.

00:49:34.903 --> 00:49:37.565
Let him die at sea.

00:49:37.625 --> 00:49:41.784
The pirates took our sailors onto their ship.

00:49:41.844 --> 00:49:44.731
They put me into a canoe.

00:49:44.791 --> 00:49:48.982
I was alone at sea, again.

00:49:49.042 --> 00:49:54.914
When I was a long way from the pirate ship, I took out my pocket telescope.

00:49:54.974 --> 00:49:58.776
Through it, I saw some small islands.

00:49:58.836 --> 00:50:03.357
I sailed towards the first island, but it was very rocky.

00:50:03.417 --> 00:50:07.808
I found some eggs, ate them, and slept under a rock.

00:50:07.868 --> 00:50:12.560
The next day, I sailed to another island, then another.

00:50:12.620 --> 00:50:16.851
On the fifth day I arrived at the last island.

00:50:16.911 --> 00:50:19.552
I found some more eggs.

00:50:19.612 --> 00:50:23.363
On this island there was a small cave.

00:50:23.423 --> 00:50:25.523
I slept a little.

00:50:25.583 --> 00:50:27.674
I was quite worried now.

00:50:27.734 --> 00:50:30.044
I was very tired.

00:50:30.104 --> 00:50:34.396
When I die here I thought.

00:50:34.456 --> 00:50:39.844
When I left the cave it was quite late the next morning.

00:50:39.904 --> 00:50:43.782
The sun was hot and the sky was clear.

00:50:43.842 --> 00:50:47.444
Suddenly it went quite dark.

00:50:47.504 --> 00:50:49.435
I looked up.

00:50:49.495 --> 00:50:53.026
There was a large cloud in the sky.

00:50:53.086 --> 00:50:57.238
But no, it wasn't a cloud.

00:50:57.299 --> 00:50:59.210
What was it?

00:50:59.270 --> 00:51:02.010
It started to come down.

00:51:02.070 --> 00:51:04.812
I took out my pocket telescope.

00:51:04.872 --> 00:51:07.593
I could see people on it.

00:51:07.653 --> 00:51:12.384
It was a very large island in the sky.

00:51:12.444 --> 00:51:17.327
I was happy to see people, so I waved and waved.

00:51:17.387 --> 00:51:20.268
Some people on the island saw me.

00:51:20.328 --> 00:51:23.300
The island came down more.

00:51:23.360 --> 00:51:26.951
More people on the island in the sky came to look.

00:51:27.011 --> 00:51:28.682
They waved at me.

00:51:28.742 --> 00:51:32.304
The island was now very near to me.

00:51:32.364 --> 00:51:36.802
Help me, help me, I shouted.

00:51:36.862 --> 00:51:41.542
The next minute I saw a seat on a rope.

00:51:41.602 --> 00:51:45.384
The seat came down from the island towards me.

00:51:45.444 --> 00:51:51.738
I sat on the seat and the people on the island pulled me up.

00:51:51.798 --> 00:51:57.890
On the island in the sky I saw some very strange people.

00:51:57.950 --> 00:52:01.178
Their eyes looked in different directions.

00:52:01.238 --> 00:52:08.358
Their clothes had a lot of symbols on them, suns, moons, stars and musical instruments.

00:52:08.418 --> 00:52:11.340
They seemed very distracted.

00:52:11.400 --> 00:52:15.304
Their servants told them when to speak and when to listen.

00:52:15.364 --> 00:52:18.606
The people on the island were very kind.

00:52:18.667 --> 00:52:22.340
They took me to the royal palace immediately.

00:52:22.400 --> 00:52:25.402
The king was also very kind.

00:52:25.462 --> 00:52:28.806
He sat on a chair in the middle of the room.

00:52:28.866 --> 00:52:32.690
there were mathematical instruments all around him.

00:52:32.750 --> 00:52:38.643
He asked me some questions, but of course I didn't understand his language.

00:52:38.703 --> 00:52:41.824
Then dinner arrived.

00:52:41.884 --> 00:52:45.136
The food was very strange.

00:52:45.196 --> 00:52:52.140
The lamb was triangular, the bread was conical, and the sausages looked like musical instruments.

00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:55.750
A group of musicians played the music.

00:52:55.810 --> 00:52:58.329
I didn't like the music at all.

00:52:58.389 --> 00:53:00.230
It was terrible.

00:53:00.290 --> 00:53:04.992
After dinner, the king sent me away with a man.

00:53:05.053 --> 00:53:07.934
He had pens and paper.

00:53:07.995 --> 00:53:10.966
He was my language teacher.

00:53:11.026 --> 00:53:17.880
He taught me the names of the shapes, the moon and stars, and all the musical instruments.

00:53:17.940 --> 00:53:23.644
After a few days, I began to understand the language.

00:53:23.704 --> 00:53:28.329
The name of the island in the sky is Laputa.

00:53:28.389 --> 00:53:32.392
Laputa flies over a larger island under it.

00:53:32.452 --> 00:53:35.603
The name of this island is Balnibabi.

00:53:35.664 --> 00:53:40.406
The capital city, Lagado, is on Balnibabi.

00:53:40.466 --> 00:53:44.358
The houses on Laputa are all very strange.

00:53:44.418 --> 00:53:48.011
There are no 90 degree angles in the houses.

00:53:48.071 --> 00:53:51.542
This is because the Laputans are not practical.

00:53:51.602 --> 00:53:56.323
They are interested in mathematics, music, and astrology.

00:53:56.383 --> 00:54:00.144
The men of Lebuta are also very scared.

00:54:00.204 --> 00:54:06.145
They are afraid that, one day, a falling star will hit their island.

00:54:06.205 --> 00:54:12.226
The women of Lebuta live a comfortable life, but they are very bored.

00:54:12.286 --> 00:54:17.057
The king uses physics to control the movement of Lebuta.

00:54:17.117 --> 00:54:22.204
He also uses Lebuta to control the people of Bowney Barbie.

00:54:22.264 --> 00:54:27.884
Dear reader, the people of Balnibarbi are very oppressed.

00:54:27.944 --> 00:54:32.928
The king can use Laputa to stop rain and block the sun.

00:54:32.988 --> 00:54:40.795
If the people of Balnibarbi cause a lot of trouble, the people of Laputa throw rocks at them.

00:54:40.855 --> 00:54:48.590
The people on the island of Laputa were kind to me, but they weren't curious about me at all.

00:54:48.650 --> 00:54:55.211
I was quite interested in both mathematics and music, but the men were quite boring.

00:54:55.271 --> 00:54:59.512
I began to talk to women, children and servants.

00:54:59.572 --> 00:55:07.974
The Leputin men were surprised at this, but the women, children and servants talked about more interesting things than the men.

00:55:08.034 --> 00:55:13.376
I studied hard, and now I could speak their language very well.

00:55:13.436 --> 00:55:16.602
But there was nothing for me here.

00:55:16.662 --> 00:55:21.308
After two months on the island, I wanted to leave.

00:55:21.368 --> 00:55:24.910
There was one Luputin man I liked.

00:55:24.970 --> 00:55:27.832
He was a very important lord.

00:55:27.892 --> 00:55:34.504
He was very intelligent, very practical, and very interested in the world around him.

00:55:34.564 --> 00:55:37.525
Everyone said he was stupid.

00:55:37.586 --> 00:55:38.936
Why?

00:55:38.996 --> 00:55:42.588
Because he didn't like Luputin music.

00:55:42.648 --> 00:55:46.112
He often came to talk to me in my room.

00:55:46.172 --> 00:55:48.575
What's Europe like?

00:55:48.635 --> 00:55:51.506
What's the legal system in England?

00:55:51.566 --> 00:55:53.656
What's Lilliput like?

00:55:53.716 --> 00:55:55.787
What's Brodynag like?

00:55:55.847 --> 00:55:57.497
He asked.

00:55:57.557 --> 00:56:01.338
One day we talked about traveling.

00:56:01.398 --> 00:56:03.298
Could you help me?

00:56:03.358 --> 00:56:04.768
I asked him.

00:56:04.828 --> 00:56:06.089
How?

00:56:06.149 --> 00:56:07.779
He answered.

00:56:07.839 --> 00:56:11.090
Will you talk to the king for me?

00:56:11.150 --> 00:56:13.224
I want to leave.

00:56:13.284 --> 00:56:18.401
I want to travel to Balnibarbi and to other places in the world.

00:56:18.461 --> 00:56:23.784
Yes, I'll talk to the king," he promised.

00:56:23.844 --> 00:56:28.457
On the 16th of February, I left Lebuta.

00:56:28.517 --> 00:56:34.591
The king gave me a present, some money, to help me on Balnibarbi.

00:56:34.650 --> 00:56:38.283
The island of Lebuta went down in the sky.

00:56:38.343 --> 00:56:44.966
When we were near Balnibarbi, I went down on the seat on the rope.

00:56:45.027 --> 00:56:52.698
Chapter 5 I visit strange and wonderful places.

00:56:52.759 --> 00:57:02.431
On Balnebabi, inside the academy, the magical island, I meet Hannibal.

00:57:02.492 --> 00:57:07.562
When I reached Balnebabi, I was very happy.

00:57:07.622 --> 00:57:10.023
I walked to Lagado.

00:57:10.083 --> 00:57:13.624
I'm sure you remember that this is the capital city.

00:57:13.684 --> 00:57:18.666
I had the name of a man to visit in Lagado, Lord Munodi.

00:57:18.726 --> 00:57:21.757
He was a friend of my friend on Laputa.

00:57:21.817 --> 00:57:24.628
The man was very happy to meet me.

00:57:24.688 --> 00:57:27.248
I stayed in his house.

00:57:27.308 --> 00:57:31.500
The next morning, he took me to visit the capital.

00:57:31.560 --> 00:57:34.841
It was about the same size as London.

00:57:34.901 --> 00:57:39.562
The houses were very strange and very badly built.

00:57:39.622 --> 00:57:42.897
The people in the streets walked fast.

00:57:42.958 --> 00:57:45.632
They looked a little wild.

00:57:45.692 --> 00:57:47.983
Their clothes were old.

00:57:48.043 --> 00:57:51.353
Then we walked into the countryside.

00:57:51.414 --> 00:57:54.594
Again, the people were poor.

00:57:54.654 --> 00:57:58.535
I was surprised because the land was good.

00:57:58.595 --> 00:58:02.246
Lord Munodi's house was different from the others.

00:58:02.306 --> 00:58:06.096
His garden was also more beautiful than the others.

00:58:06.156 --> 00:58:09.922
I asked Lord Munodi why.

00:58:09.982 --> 00:58:16.369
About 40 years ago, the Leputin government built an academy here in Lagado.

00:58:16.429 --> 00:58:20.541
The academy studies building, agriculture and languages.

00:58:20.601 --> 00:58:23.942
The professors have some very strange ideas.

00:58:24.002 --> 00:58:29.874
They tell the Leputin government their ideas and the government makes stupid laws.

00:58:29.934 --> 00:58:31.826
They are not practical.

00:58:31.886 --> 00:58:36.847
My house is different because I break the laws.

00:58:36.907 --> 00:58:39.618
Can I visit the academy?"

00:58:39.678 --> 00:58:40.658
I asked.

00:58:40.718 --> 00:58:44.870
Yes, about you must go alone," he answered.

00:58:44.930 --> 00:58:49.323
I hate the academy, and I will never ever go there.

00:58:49.383 --> 00:58:51.734
You must take some money with you.

00:58:51.794 --> 00:58:57.438
They never have any money for their studies, so they beg from visitors.

00:58:57.498 --> 00:59:01.550
The following day I visited the academy.

00:59:01.610 --> 00:59:04.719
The dean was very happy to meet me.

00:59:04.779 --> 00:59:09.998
The academy was very large with about 500 rooms.

00:59:10.058 --> 00:59:14.150
In the first room, there was an old man.

00:59:14.210 --> 00:59:17.322
He told me about his studies.

00:59:17.382 --> 00:59:21.464
I'm working on a very important project.

00:59:21.524 --> 00:59:25.575
I'm trying to make sunlight from cucumbers.

00:59:25.635 --> 00:59:33.597
We take the sunlight out of the cucumbers, put it in a bottle, and then we can use it on cold days.

00:59:33.657 --> 00:59:36.748
Very interesting, I said.

00:59:36.808 --> 00:59:39.110
I gave him some money.

00:59:39.170 --> 00:59:41.622
I went into another room.

00:59:41.682 --> 00:59:45.716
The smell was so bad that I left immediately.

00:59:45.776 --> 00:59:50.310
In another room, there was a very clever engineer.

00:59:50.370 --> 00:59:53.744
He had a new way of building houses.

00:59:53.804 --> 00:59:58.248
He built the roof first and the walls second.

00:59:58.308 --> 01:00:02.054
At the end, he built the foundations.

01:00:02.114 --> 01:00:06.539
In the next room there was a man who couldn't see.

01:00:06.599 --> 01:00:10.312
His job was to mix colours for artists.

01:00:10.372 --> 01:00:14.294
He did this by smell and by touch.

01:00:14.354 --> 01:00:21.478
I visited a lot of rooms in the academy, but I didn't see any practical ideas.

01:00:21.538 --> 01:00:26.332
The dean wanted to show me more rooms on the other side of the academy.

01:00:26.392 --> 01:00:29.413
There I visited the school of languages.

01:00:29.473 --> 01:00:32.102
There were three professors there.

01:00:32.163 --> 01:00:36.172
Their job was to improve their language.

01:00:36.232 --> 01:00:39.272
What exactly are you doing?

01:00:39.332 --> 01:00:41.634
I asked one professor.

01:00:41.694 --> 01:00:45.235
This is my language machine, he answered.

01:00:45.295 --> 01:00:47.666
It's making our words shorter.

01:00:47.726 --> 01:00:51.297
All words will soon be very, very short.

01:00:51.357 --> 01:00:54.578
Very interesting, I said.

01:00:54.638 --> 01:01:00.162
My job is more interesting, said the second professor.

01:01:00.222 --> 01:01:04.106
There is no need for words in our language.

01:01:04.167 --> 01:01:07.278
Speaking is very bad for people.

01:01:07.338 --> 01:01:10.209
Too much speaking makes people ill.

01:01:10.269 --> 01:01:13.940
In my system, we don't need words.

01:01:14.000 --> 01:01:15.911
We need things.

01:01:15.971 --> 01:01:21.194
People will soon communicate by carrying things in their pockets.

01:01:21.254 --> 01:01:25.798
For short conversations, you only need a few things.

01:01:25.858 --> 01:01:31.652
Of course, for long conversations, you need servants to carry your things.

01:01:31.712 --> 01:01:36.666
For very long conversations, you just need a cart.

01:01:36.726 --> 01:01:39.898
My system has one great advantage.

01:01:39.958 --> 01:01:42.770
It's a universal language.

01:01:42.830 --> 01:01:46.964
You can communicate with people from all over the world.

01:01:47.024 --> 01:01:51.557
But my language machine is the best," said the first professor.

01:01:51.577 --> 01:01:57.342
"'No, yours is too complicated," said the second.

01:01:57.402 --> 01:02:01.734
I gave them some money and left quickly.

01:02:01.794 --> 01:02:07.088
Next, I spent a very short time at the School of Mathematics.

01:02:07.148 --> 01:02:11.650
There the scientists wrote formulas on edible paper.

01:02:11.710 --> 01:02:15.304
They then ate them immediately.

01:02:15.364 --> 01:02:20.350
I now understood that all these professors were mad.

01:02:20.410 --> 01:02:26.976
Balnebabi was poor and unhappy because of these professors and their silly ideas.

01:02:27.036 --> 01:02:32.140
I decided to leave the academy and Balnebabi as soon as possible.

01:02:32.200 --> 01:02:35.483
I wanted to go back to Europe.

01:02:35.543 --> 01:02:39.756
The next day, I spoke to Lord Munodi.

01:02:39.816 --> 01:02:42.980
I want to go back to England, I said.

01:02:43.040 --> 01:02:45.963
I'm not surprised," he answered.

01:02:46.023 --> 01:02:47.774
Perhaps I can help.

01:02:47.834 --> 01:02:52.818
The King of Lugnag has a very good relationship with the Emperor of Japan.

01:02:52.879 --> 01:02:58.042
It must be possible to get from there to Japan and from Japan to England.

01:02:58.102 --> 01:03:00.294
Why don't you go to Lugnag?

01:03:00.355 --> 01:03:03.606
It's a small island, and it's quite near.

01:03:03.666 --> 01:03:05.688
Thank you, I said.

01:03:05.748 --> 01:03:08.160
That's a very good idea.

01:03:08.221 --> 01:03:12.900
I said goodbye to Lord Munodie and left Lagado.

01:03:12.960 --> 01:03:16.447
I traveled to the port of Maldonada.

01:03:16.508 --> 01:03:20.900
When I arrived, I spoke to a man at the port.

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:23.252
When's the next ship for Lugnag?

01:03:23.312 --> 01:03:24.352
I asked.

01:03:24.413 --> 01:03:27.804
In five weeks, he answered.

01:03:27.864 --> 01:03:33.968
I decided to spend the time visiting a different island, Club Dubdrib.

01:03:34.028 --> 01:03:37.860
Its other name is the Magical Island.

01:03:37.920 --> 01:03:40.353
It's a very small island.

01:03:40.414 --> 01:03:44.026
The king of the Magical Island is a magician.

01:03:44.086 --> 01:03:46.898
He has a very special power.

01:03:46.958 --> 01:03:51.190
He can call ghosts from the past to be his servants.

01:03:51.250 --> 01:03:55.102
They can only work for him for 24 hours.

01:03:55.163 --> 01:04:01.056
When I arrived at the Magical Island, I went immediately to see the king.

01:04:01.116 --> 01:04:06.960
He was very happy to see me and invited me to stay at the Royal Palace.

01:04:07.020 --> 01:04:12.563
It was a little strange at first, because the servants were always different.

01:04:12.624 --> 01:04:17.306
One evening, the king invited me to a special dinner.

01:04:17.366 --> 01:04:20.848
After dinner, we talked.

01:04:20.908 --> 01:04:24.710
I like you, Galiva, he said.

01:04:24.770 --> 01:04:27.182
I have an interesting idea.

01:04:27.242 --> 01:04:30.373
Do you want to meet some people from the past?

01:04:30.434 --> 01:04:33.275
Yes, please, I replied.

01:04:33.335 --> 01:04:34.926
Who?

01:04:34.986 --> 01:04:37.252
Let me think.

01:04:37.312 --> 01:04:40.528
Alexander the Great, I answered.

01:04:40.588 --> 01:04:45.219
Call him, then he will appear, said the king.

01:04:45.279 --> 01:04:49.180
Alexander the Great, I called.

01:04:49.240 --> 01:04:53.441
Two seconds later Alexander appeared.

01:04:53.501 --> 01:04:57.542
It was difficult to understand his Greek at first.

01:04:57.603 --> 01:05:00.783
Another, said the king.

01:05:00.843 --> 01:05:03.788
Soon Hannibal appeared.

01:05:03.848 --> 01:05:05.091
Look!

01:05:05.151 --> 01:05:08.722
He's crossing the Alps, I shouted.

01:05:08.783 --> 01:05:12.294
I then asked to see Caesar and Pompey.

01:05:12.354 --> 01:05:15.976
Then the whole Senate of Rome appeared.

01:05:16.036 --> 01:05:18.896
Caesar and Brutus came near to me.

01:05:18.956 --> 01:05:23.198
I spoke to Brutus, a very fine man.

01:05:23.258 --> 01:05:27.840
The next day I decided to call some more ghosts.

01:05:27.900 --> 01:05:31.001
Homer and Aristotle were interesting.

01:05:31.061 --> 01:05:34.144
I called Descartes and Gascendi.

01:05:34.204 --> 01:05:36.956
Aristotle was pleased to meet them.

01:05:37.016 --> 01:05:45.052
Oh dear, I made some mistakes in my philosophy, he said, after a long conversation.

01:05:45.112 --> 01:05:49.884
The next day I called some ghosts from modern history.

01:05:49.944 --> 01:05:52.556
They were very disappointing.

01:05:52.616 --> 01:05:56.769
I called people from the past and recent past.

01:05:56.829 --> 01:05:58.870
It was strange.

01:05:58.930 --> 01:06:03.629
All the people from the recent past were very disappointing.

01:06:03.689 --> 01:06:13.292
At the end of my stay on the magical island, I understood more about the problems of my country and the problems of Europe.

01:06:13.352 --> 01:06:16.606
It was time for me to leave.

01:06:16.666 --> 01:06:22.410
I thanked the king of the magical island very much and went back to Maldonada.

01:06:22.470 --> 01:06:25.642
There I found a ship for Lugnag.

01:06:25.702 --> 01:06:28.422
The journey took a month.

01:06:28.482 --> 01:06:36.023
It is easy to communicate with the people of Lugnag because many of them speak the language of Balnibabi.

01:06:36.083 --> 01:06:39.995
The Lugnagians are very polite, generous people.

01:06:40.055 --> 01:06:43.056
They all seem to be very happy.

01:06:43.116 --> 01:06:48.750
Soon after I arrived, the king invited me to the royal palace.

01:06:48.810 --> 01:06:54.442
I wanted to be polite too, so I learnt some words in Lugnagian.

01:06:54.502 --> 01:06:59.158
When I arrived at the palace, I said these words to the king.

01:06:59.218 --> 01:07:06.814
Ickling-gloth-robs-gud-serum-blah-he-ob-mash-nout-zwind-mod-balk-guf-slyob-had-gud-lobasht.

01:07:06.874 --> 01:07:09.264
He was very pleased.

01:07:09.324 --> 01:07:12.795
He invited me to stay in the royal palace.

01:07:12.855 --> 01:07:15.866
I stayed for three months.

01:07:15.926 --> 01:07:20.707
One day a lug-nag-ian asked me a strange question.

01:07:20.767 --> 01:07:23.778
Would you like to meet any mortal?

01:07:23.838 --> 01:07:25.780
What do you mean?

01:07:25.841 --> 01:07:28.564
Some people here are immortal.

01:07:28.624 --> 01:07:30.716
They live forever."

01:07:30.776 --> 01:07:33.508
How wonderful, I said.

01:07:33.569 --> 01:07:37.452
Yes, I would like to learn from any mortal.

01:07:37.512 --> 01:07:40.014
They will teach me a lot about life.

01:07:40.074 --> 01:07:43.396
Perhaps I can learn something special.

01:07:43.456 --> 01:07:48.600
Unfortunately, the immortals are not nice people.

01:07:48.660 --> 01:07:55.907
They are angry, horrible, jealous, miserable, and extremely talkative.

01:07:55.967 --> 01:08:00.800
Because they are different from other people, they don't have friends.

01:08:00.860 --> 01:08:03.641
They are also very ugly.

01:08:03.702 --> 01:08:07.483
They have a strange blue spot on their heads.

01:08:07.543 --> 01:08:11.795
The oldest immortal I met was 200 years old.

01:08:11.855 --> 01:08:17.547
He was very, very angry and very, very horrible.

01:08:17.607 --> 01:08:22.979
I began to understand that the Lugnagians don't like the Immortals.

01:08:23.039 --> 01:08:25.687
They don't want to live forever.

01:08:25.747 --> 01:08:31.097
Perhaps that's why the Loughnagians are so happy.

01:08:31.157 --> 01:08:37.042
After three months at the Royal Palace, I decided to leave.

01:08:37.101 --> 01:08:40.644
It was time to go back to England and my family.

01:08:40.703 --> 01:08:42.955
The king was sorry.

01:08:43.015 --> 01:08:45.616
Stay here, he said.

01:08:45.676 --> 01:08:48.409
You can work for my government.

01:08:48.468 --> 01:08:51.101
I'm sorry, I answered.

01:08:51.160 --> 01:08:52.891
I must go home.

01:08:52.952 --> 01:08:55.900
I must see my family again.

01:08:55.960 --> 01:08:58.799
The king was very generous.

01:08:58.859 --> 01:09:04.040
He gave me some gold and a beautiful red diamond.

01:09:04.101 --> 01:09:08.102
In early May, I left Lugnag.

01:09:08.162 --> 01:09:11.283
I arrived in Japan two weeks later.

01:09:11.343 --> 01:09:16.255
In Japan, I began to look for a ship to take me to Europe.

01:09:16.315 --> 01:09:19.646
It was very difficult to find a ship.

01:09:19.706 --> 01:09:23.458
After a few weeks, I found a Dutch ship.

01:09:23.518 --> 01:09:25.908
I spoke to the captain.

01:09:25.967 --> 01:09:27.918
Where are you from?"

01:09:27.978 --> 01:09:29.238
he asked.

01:09:29.298 --> 01:09:31.919
Holland, I answered.

01:09:31.979 --> 01:09:36.020
The Dutch and the English weren't good friends at this time.

01:09:36.080 --> 01:09:38.281
It was better to be Dutch.

01:09:38.341 --> 01:09:42.632
Luckily, I knew the Dutch language very well.

01:09:42.692 --> 01:09:47.564
Captain Theodoras Van Groot was happy to take me.

01:09:47.624 --> 01:09:49.895
He needed a ship's doctor.

01:09:49.955 --> 01:09:54.136
I invented some stories about my family in Gholderland.

01:09:54.196 --> 01:09:57.638
No one knew I was English.

01:09:57.698 --> 01:10:02.202
In June, we finally left Japan.

01:10:02.262 --> 01:10:06.194
The journey was long, but there were no adventures.

01:10:06.254 --> 01:10:09.066
We stopped at the Cape of Good Hope.

01:10:09.126 --> 01:10:14.210
This time, we only stayed for two days because the weather was good.

01:10:14.270 --> 01:10:18.753
We got fresh water and sailed away immediately.

01:10:18.813 --> 01:10:24.437
On the 6th of April, 1710, we arrived at Amsterdam.

01:10:24.497 --> 01:10:28.544
I immediately found another boat from Amsterdam to England.

01:10:28.604 --> 01:10:31.839
Four days later, I was home.

01:10:31.899 --> 01:10:35.262
My wife was very happy to see me.

01:10:35.322 --> 01:10:40.155
She was very well, and so were my children.

01:10:40.215 --> 01:10:45.548
I stayed at home in England for five very happy months.

01:10:45.608 --> 01:10:49.772
Then, I started to think about traveling again.

01:10:49.832 --> 01:10:52.974
I spoke to some friends.

01:10:53.034 --> 01:10:57.337
Didn't you sail on the adventure a few years ago?

01:10:57.397 --> 01:11:00.996
One of them said, Yes, why?

01:11:01.055 --> 01:11:04.167
Well, they need a new captain.

01:11:04.227 --> 01:11:06.838
Why don't you speak to the owner?

01:11:06.898 --> 01:11:11.730
I traveled to Portsmouth to meet the owner of the adventure.

01:11:11.790 --> 01:11:17.802
After many years as a ship's doctor, I understood navigation very well.

01:11:17.862 --> 01:11:21.754
It was time for me to become the captain of a ship.

01:11:21.814 --> 01:11:23.815
The owner was happy.

01:11:23.875 --> 01:11:26.176
He remembered me from before.

01:11:26.236 --> 01:11:29.500
The job is yours, he said.

01:11:29.559 --> 01:11:32.223
I was very pleased.

01:11:32.283 --> 01:11:35.424
Now I needed a ship's doctor.

01:11:35.485 --> 01:11:37.336
I found a young man.

01:11:37.396 --> 01:11:39.757
He was very good at his job.

01:11:39.817 --> 01:11:43.789
Then I said goodbye to my wife and children.

01:11:43.849 --> 01:11:48.642
We left Portsmouth on the 7th of September, 1710.

01:11:48.702 --> 01:11:50.782
Our destination?

01:11:50.842 --> 01:11:52.654
The South Seas.

01:11:52.714 --> 01:11:53.334
Again.

